invariant: INV-16
file: p256_sign.c
catches: p256_sign_test
reason: generator_update writes a new K and keeps the midstates of the
  old one, so every HMAC after the first update runs under a key RFC 6979
  never named (docs/decisions.md 147). Every nonce is then a function of
  the private key and the message still, so a signature verifies, and a
  test that checks only verification passes. The RFC 6979 vectors in
  bin/p256_sign_test pin each signature's bytes.

--- old
    memcpy(g->k, next, SHA256_LEN);
    generator_key(cpu, g);
--- new
    memcpy(g->k, next, SHA256_LEN);
